# Line endings, decided once for everyone who clones this.
#
# Without this file the repository's contents depend on each contributor's
# local git settings. Two things go wrong, and only one of them is cosmetic:
#
#  * A clone on Windows checks out CRLF. Any other tool looking at that
#    working tree - a container, a CI runner, a second git with different
#    settings - reports every file as modified, and the real change you were
#    looking for is buried in twenty-one files of noise.
#
#  * A shell script committed with CRLF fails on Linux with "bad interpreter:
#    No such file or directory", which names the wrong problem entirely and
#    costs somebody an afternoon.
#
# So: everything is stored as LF, checked out however the platform likes.
* text=auto

# Except these, which are executed rather than read. They are LF on disk on
# every platform, because the kernel reads the shebang literally.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Not text. Never touch these.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.pdf binary
*.bundle binary
